{
  "run_cypher": [
    "Optional explicit graph_v1 selection; language features are inferred from the query. Existing scalar SQL queries retain their execution path. Bounded evaluation supports CASE/nullable booleans, arithmetic, lists/maps, list comprehensions, all/any/none/single, registered scalar and temporal functions, and aggregates inside scalar/map/list expressions (count/sum/avg/min/max/collect/stdev/stdevp/percentileCont/percentileDisc). Temporal values use ISO text and logical value_types; IANA zone rules use host tzdb. WITH, MATCH, OPTIONAL MATCH and UNWIND execute in order (64 stages, 32 UNWINDs). WITH replaces scope and supports aliases, aggregate filtering and local pagination. UNION/UNION ALL allow 32 independently scoped branches with identical column names; mixing operators is refused. The default 1000-row cap applies after union evaluation. Pagination accepts nonnegative integer parameters or row-independent expressions. Patterns support typed/untyped nodes, direct relationship type alternatives, named undirected relationships, fixed/variable paths, nodes()/relationships()/length(), pattern comprehensions/predicates and correlated EXISTS, including nested queries. Each MATCH enforces relationship uniqueness. Explicit path bounds cannot exceed eight hops; an unbounded traversal that can exceed eight fails instead of truncating. Nodes have one BKN object type. A direct relation is a virtual endpoint join fact, with no independently stored properties or parallel edge identities. properties(r) is empty and r.property is null. Native multi-label/parallel/property-bearing edge fixtures are not applicable to this graph contract. Writes and procedures are refused. Graph-valued CASE/coalesce/head/last/list/path operations preserve property origins. All stages, branches and correlated observations are compiled and authorized before reads, including lazy/empty branches. Query dependencies do not expand public object snapshots. object_properties names MATCH node variables, not WITH aliases. Graph binding requires full readable complete primary keys. Generic patterns scan bounded authorized type/relation observations before correlation and cache them per request; selective output may still exceed the scan budget. No datasource transaction snapshot is guaranteed. The request shares 9999 work rows, 8 MiB assembly, 79992 iterations/comparisons and a 30-second timeout. Each pattern allows at most 64 typed observations. Incomplete reads or budget overflow fail the entire query. This is a bounded BKN implementation, not a full read-only TCK certification. Supports DISTINCT, ORDER BY and count(*) * 2. Unsupported: CREATE/MERGE/DELETE/SET/REMOVE and CALL.",
    "WITH/OPTIONAL MATCH/UNWIND/UNION preserve clause order and variable scope. Use keyword arguments for object_properties and result_format."
